maya: Quick sync on TitanCorp dedicated bring-up. Quota signed off for the reserved pool (20k RPS equiv). Need someone to own autoscale policy + a short loadtest window. Who can pick this up?

omar: I can own autoscale policy. What are the p95 latency targets and any GPU preferences? Also need expected request size distribution to tune batching.

maya: Target p95 <= 150ms for text-gen endpoints. Customer prefers p4d for latency but open to a100 if cost constrained. Traffic split estimate: ~30% short (<32 tokens), 50% medium (32-256), 20% long (>256).

jia: I'll run the load tests (shadow first). Plan: `k6` ramp test to validate autoscale then a 2-hr soak. Need a sample traffic file + ephemeral API token. Suggest start: `k6 run --vus 2000 --duration 15m script.js` then step to peak.

maya: Sample traffic link: https://internal-artifacts/titancorp/traffic-samples.csv (internal). Do NOT post tokens here — @ops-bot create ephemeral creds for jia. Also want a warmup plan: prime KV cache and run prefix-caching for top 20 prompts.

ops-bot: Secret request created: req-83423 (ephemeral token for jia, expires in 4 hours).

julian: A couple of SRE notes: set scale-up cooldown 30s, scale-down cooldown 120s. Use both GPU memory pressure and queue length as triggers. Add graceful fallback policy to route to `redwood-medium` if available capacity drops below 15%. Also include steady-state batching target (tokens-per-batch ~ 6-8 for medium requests).

omar: Good call. I'll draft the HPA-like policy and include mem+queue triggers + fallback model. Also add a soft cap on concurrent streams per GPU to avoid OOMs.

jia: I'll prepare the k6 scripts and a small harness that rotates through the sample CSV and tags requests for latency buckets. Example snippet for circling tokens:```js
import http from 'k6/http';
import { sleep } from 'k6';
const data = open('traffic.csv');
export default function() {
  const body = { input: randomLine(data) };
  http.post('https://api.redwood.example/v1/generate', JSON.stringify(body), { headers: { 'Authorization': `Bearer ${__ENV.TOKEN}` } });
  sleep(0.02);
}
```

maya: Proposed soak window: Wed 03:00-05:00 UTC (low production impact). Can we confirm runbook items: run smoke 30m, ramp 30m, soak 60m; observe p95, GPU mem, and fallback events. @omar @jia confirm?

omar: Confirmed, I'll open PR with policy and a checklist by EOD. :thumbsup:

jia: Confirmed, will post final `k6` command and resource expectation graphs in the runbook channel before the test.

maya: Awesome — I'll loop in customer success lead for TitanCorp to set expectation and get approval for the window. Thanks everyone.
